**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExperimentMatrixTests`

**How to implement.** The experiment matrix as pure Domain: rows source × objects × φ, columns analyzer, each cell the experiments measured there (001 §O 'Experiment matrix view: rows source × objects × φ, columns analyzer, with a data badge per cell'; the S9.3 brief; step 268's reading of 001's words: the source is the polarization source, the Prep slots). The view and its badges are step 327's. New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentMatrices.fs`: `module ExperimentMatrices` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `DataSplits.fs` (step 317): one `<Compile>` line in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` and no comment. Its module doc is one to three lines citing 001 §O and spec 0050 S9.3, and each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. In this order: (1) `MatrixObject = { item : ItemLabel; angle : Angle }`, an object slot's item and its angle (`SetupSlot.turnAngle`, step 277: a dial reading, else R1). (2) `MatrixRowKey = { sources : ItemLabel list; objects : MatrixObject list }` and `MatrixColumnKey = { analyzers : ItemLabel list }`. (3) `MatrixCell = { row : MatrixRowKey; column : MatrixColumnKey; experiments : Experiments.ExperimentId list }`. (4) `ExperimentMatrix = { rows : MatrixRowKey list; columns : MatrixColumnKey list; cells : MatrixCell list; unplaced : Experiments.ExperimentId list }`, with `member this.tryFindCell (row : MatrixRowKey) (column : MatrixColumnKey) : MatrixCell option` and `static member ofExperiments (experiments : Experiment list) (setups : Setup list) (items : Item list) : ExperimentMatrix`, the one rule: for each experiment in order, `experiment.slotsIn setups` (step 261); an error puts its id in `unplaced`. Its slots in light order (`SetupSlot.inLightOrder`, step 257) give: `sources`, the labels of the items the `PrepSlotRole` slots hold; `objects`, for each `ObjectSlotRole` slot holding an item, its label and the slot's `turnAngle`; and the column's `analyzers`, the labels of the items the `AnalyzerSlotRole` slots hold, each list in light order. A slot holding nothing, or an item `items` lacks, adds nothing; the source and detector slots do not enter. Rows and columns are listed in the order they first appear, and a cell holds the ids of its experiments in the collection's order, cells listed in the order their first experiment appears. No sort, cache, text or other member is added: captions are the view's (step 327). Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentMatrixTests.fs`, `module ExperimentMatrixTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, over test-local copies of step 271's slots and items (`Laser`, `CPL1`, `CPL2`, `QZ`, `LR`, `QZd` dial-mounted with its zero at 10°): `the matrix puts each experiment in the row of its sources and objects at their angles and the column of its analyzers`: setups `A` (`lpA` `CPL1`, `sampleA` `QZ` at R1 45°, `lpB` `CPL2`), `B` (the same with `QZ` at 90°) and `C` (as `A` with `lpB` empty), and experiments E1 over A, E2 over B, E3 over A and E4 over C, give the rows `CPL1 · QZ@45` and `CPL1 · QZ@90` and the columns `[CPL2]` and `[]`, in that order, and the cells (row 1, `[CPL2]`) = [E1; E3], (row 2, `[CPL2]`) = [E2] and (row 1, `[]`) = [E4]; `tryFindCell` of row 2 and `[]` answers `None`. `two objects in series make one row, a dial-mounted object sits at its reading, and an experiment whose setup the kit lacks is unplaced`: a setup with `QZ` at 45° in `sampleA` and `LR` at 45° in `sampleB` gives one row whose objects are `QZ@45` then `LR@45`; `QZd` in `sampleA` at R1 30° sits at −20°; and an experiment over `Gone` revision 1 is in `unplaced` and in no cell.

**Acceptance.** After the matrix lands, `ExperimentMatrix.ofExperiments` MUST place each experiment in the row of its Prep items and its objects at their angles and the column of its analyzers, in first-appearance order, and list every experiment whose setup the kit lacks as unplaced; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the matrix puts each experiment in the row of its sources and objects at their angles and the column of its analyzers` and `two objects in series make one row, a dial-mounted object sits at its reading, and an experiment whose setup the kit lacks is unplaced`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.
